B15:
Per-instance Scripts (610 copies): every copy is duplicated code - a bug fix means editing hundreds of scripts (or packages), each runs its own thread/connections and memory, startup cost, inconsistent versions, hard to tune globally, and scripts inside models that stream/clone/destroy behave unpredictably.
Tag-driven: tag instances with CollectionService ("Door", "Pickup", "Turret"), and have one server Script/module per kind (or one loader requiring a component module per tag) that:
- iterates CollectionService:GetTagged(tag) at start and connects GetInstanceAddedSignal(tag) for newly spawned or streamed-in instances, setting up a component (state + connections) per instance;
- connects GetInstanceRemovedSignal(tag) to clean up (disconnect, clear table entries) when destroyed, untagged or streamed out;
- keeps config in attributes on the instance (e.g. Damage, Range, Respawn) so designers tune without code.
Turrets can share one Heartbeat loop that iterates active turrets (and throttles far/idle ones) instead of 60 loops. Server owns gameplay (doors' state, pickup grants, turret targeting/damage); clients use their own tag listeners for visuals only, which naturally handles StreamingEnabled since tagged instances fire Added when streamed in and Removed when streamed out. Tags replicate, set them in Studio (Tag Editor) or on spawn before parenting.
